# The thumbnail view over a lot of files, which is this app's own scrolling code.
#
# The tile panel is a VirtualizingWrapPanel written here rather than a WPF one, because a WrapPanel
# is not a virtualizing panel: it built a container for every row, and every container asks for a
# thumbnail the moment it exists. Measured over a flat branch view of a thousand videos, the
# details list took 3.9 s and the same listing as tiles never finished inside a four-minute
# watchdog. So what this script is really asserting is that the replacement puts the right things
# in the right places — the part a stopwatch cannot tell you.
#
# Every fourth file is a .txt, which draws as a full-width row instead of a tile. The sort bands
# media to the end in this view, so the rows all land before the tiles rather than between them —
# but the panel does not know that, and lays lines out for either. What this fixture does prove is
# that the two shapes measure differently and the grid still lines up underneath them.

many-fixture 800
go Many
flat all
assert-count 808

# --- Details first, as the baseline: the same rows, the panel WPF supplies ---

assert-realized under 200
shot 01-details

# --- Tiles ---

thumbnails 0.5
assert-count 808
# The whole point: 808 rows, a screenful of containers.
assert-realized under 200
shot 02-tiles-top

# --- Scrolled. Nothing here synthesises a wheel, so this drives the ScrollViewer, which is
#     the same IScrollInfo a wheel would reach. ---

list-scroll 4000
assert-realized under 200
shot 03-tiles-scrolled

list-scroll 100000
assert-realized under 200
shot 04-tiles-bottom

list-scroll 0
shot 05-tiles-back-at-top

# --- Revealing a row far down has to bring it into view, which for a virtualized item means
#     scrolling from the index alone: there is no element yet to bring anywhere. `select` on its
#     own deliberately does not scroll — clicking a row cannot, since you had to see it first. ---

reveal clip0798.mp4
assert-selected 1
shot 06-tiles-revealed

# --- Resizing the tiles re-flows every line, and the panel has to believe the new size ---

thumbnails 1
assert-count 808
assert-realized under 200
shot 07-tiles-large

thumbnails 0
assert-count 808
assert-not-launched
state
